<title>UK: BT says rules out legal action on windfall tax.</title>
<headline>BT says rules out legal action on windfall tax.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc said on Thursday that its board has decided not to challenge the validity of the windfall tax announced by the Chancellor of the Exchequer earlier this month.</p>
<p>&quot;We estimate the windfall tax announced by the Chancellor in his budget will result in a charge to BT of around 500 million pounds,&quot; a BT spokesman said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;This will be taken as a charge against profits in the three months to September 1997 and will be paid in two equal instalments in December 1997 and December 1998.&quot;</p>
</text>
